    "durationMs": 333956,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete. The full harness flow (`sh start.sh` → build → migrate → serve on 0.0.0.0:8000) verified end-to-end, then I stopped the server and reset the database to a clean state.\n\n**What was built:**\n\n- **API routes** (`src/links/`): `POST /links` (201 with `{code, url, clicks:0}`, auto-generated 8-char codes when omitted), `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}` (302 + `Location`, atomic SQL increment so clicks count exactly once per request), `GET /links` (`{items, total}` in ascending creation order)\n- **Error contract**: global exception filter + custom ValidationPipe exception factory map malformed JSON, missing/invalid `url`, and invalid `code` to 422; duplicate custom code → 409; unknown codes → 404 — all with an `error` field\n- **Persistence**: TypeORM 0.3 + pg against `DATABASE_URL` (no hardcoded credentials), `Link` entity with a unique `code` column, serial ids, `clicks` counter\n- **Migrations**: `CreateLinks` migration applied by `start.sh` via the TypeORM CLI; idempotent on restart\n- **Durability**: verified links and click counts survive a real server restart (clicks persisted 1 → 2 across restart, then 3)\n- **start.sh**: compiles TS, runs pending migrations, execs `node dist/main.js` in the foreground — no dependency installation inside\n- **README**: includes a \"Starting the server\" section covering `npm install`, `DATABASE_URL`, and `sh start.sh`\n\nOne nuance found during testing: WHATWG's URL parser accepts inputs like `http:///path` (host inferred as `path`), so those are valid by spec; `http://` without a host correctly returns 422."
  }
